WEBVTT

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:07.670
Rage of Bahamut

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:25.790
TEMPLE ARK

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.540
-What is it?
-Enemy attack!

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.880
Could it be the demons?

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.910
No, they should not have the forces necessary
to be attacking our sanctuary.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:17.770
It's the humans!

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.570
The humans are attacking!

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:05.720
I knew it was you vile humans.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.320
You use the powers forbidden by the gods...

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.490
...and continue to attack our holy sanctuaries.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.530
You arrogant creatures.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:20.100
Do not make the mistake of believing
that you humans will be able...

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.740
...to handle such power.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:39.620
The age of man revering the gods has ended.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:48.030
Royal Capital Anatae

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:12.050
They've all got big wings.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:17.890
Rest assured, they will be cleanly removed
before you receive them.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:24.400
What's going on?

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:31.440
It's him. It's the rag demon.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.650
Curses!

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.480
Take this.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:24.190
W-- Wait. Don't kill me.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:27.860
Hold there!

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.620
-Morning.
-Good morning.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:04.890
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.630
-Morning.
-Good morning.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.600
Good morning.

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:13.970
-Morning.
-Oh, good morning.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.200
You're full of energy this morning, Nina.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:19.110
Yeah, I can't wait to get to work.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:22.280
Good. I have a present for such a diligent worker.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:24.180
Take it with you.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:26.010
Thanks!

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:31.620
Smells so good.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:40.190
You really love to eat.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:43.930
-Lord Charioce has returned!
-He's returned?

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:46.800
Oh, I don't want to miss it.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.570
All hail Lord Charioce!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.210
All hail Lord Charioce!

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.880
I'm going to be busy repairing their swords.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:59.950
But first, they'll need to celebrate their triumphant return,
which means a big order of meats.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.580
We're so blessed.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:04.120
Hey, what's so great about this?

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:07.590
The reason I'm able
to share the bread like that with you...

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:11.890
...is all thanks to Lord Charioce XVII, King of Anatae.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:16.960
The capital has prospered so much
under Lord Charioce.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.630
You should be grateful to the king.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.640
I'm grateful then.

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:50.600
Check that--

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.370
You there.

00:06:57.710 --> 00:07:00.110
Up here.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:03.710
Could you come up here
and help me move this scaffolding?

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.680
Okay.

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:11.290
Where do you want it?

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:13.750
Right here.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:19.730
You're quite strong. I haven't seen you around.
Are you new to Anatae?

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:21.730
-Yeah.
-What's your name?

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:23.400
Nina.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:26.370
"Nina." That's a good name.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.100
Where are you from?

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:31.340
Where are you from?

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:33.710
Where are you from?

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:38.210
What does that matter?

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.210
What's wrong?

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:46.150
Anyway, those people over there
are really hard workers.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.320
Those aren't people.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:51.030
-Keep pulling!
-They're not people?

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:54.730
I wouldn't think about them too much.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:58.230
These are just the times we live in.

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:09.440
No! No!

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:13.080
You're pretty bashful, aren't you, Nina?

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.320
That's a big picture.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:25.390
Is that the king?

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:26.930
That's right.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:30.700
I saw the king for the first time this morning.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:36.770
Everyone was saying that
Charioce XVII is a great king.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.040
What's that?

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:42.080
That's Bahamut.

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:43.910
Bahamut?

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.110
How old were you 10 years ago?

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:48.250
Six.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:51.990
Then you should remember Bahamut.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:53.820
Yeah.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:58.790
Ten years ago,
the fireballs rained down on my village too.

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:07.200
Bahamut turned the continent of Mistarcia
into a wasteland.

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:12.270
Those who lived through it
will undoubtedly never forget the fear of Bahamut.

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:18.480
And it was Charioce XVII who resurrected
the Royal Capital Anatae from that despair.

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:21.320
And this mural is telling that history?

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:24.950
That's right. It's our king's great history.

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:29.290
By the way, Nina,
did you come to the capital to earn money?

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:30.760
Yeah.

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:33.290
I want to give my mom a better life.

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:40.800
While the capital gets to flourish,
my village has stayed poor these past 10 years.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:44.840
It's not like the capital isn't without its problems.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:46.470
Really?

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:06.190
Kaisar.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.560
My Lord.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:09.800
Look at them.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.800
They are fighting for their lives.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:17.200
I heard you allowed the rag demon
to escape again last night.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.880
Do not disappoint me.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:31.820
Yes, my Lord.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:40.030
Hey, take care of this.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.100
Mugaro.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:22.870
Rage of Bahamut

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:26.310
I'm home.

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:32.980
Don't give me that "I'm home" crap.
You've been crashing here for 10 days.

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:35.150
Get out of here already, you idiot.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:39.150
Now, now, now. Calm down, Bacchus.

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:44.320
This is a place for bounty hunters.
Not a shelter for brats like you.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:47.130
Excuse me, but I am a bounty hunter.

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:50.630
What? But you've never collected a single bounty.

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:53.570
Don't worry, I'll get me a big one sooner or later.

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:57.340
Someone so big it'll make you cry, boss.

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:59.240
But until then, I'll be staying here.

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:01.540
That's not up to you.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:07.080
Besides, even though you're guys,
it doesn't affect me at all.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:12.920
Anyway, looks like this guy's bounty went up again.

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:16.460
Seems like nobody has been able to catch him.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.660
He doesn't look that strong.

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:22.630
Apparently, he caused some trouble last night too.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:28.570
They say that he always appears
whenever slave traders and the like abuse any demons.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:30.000
Is he a good guy?

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:34.940
How can a bounty be a good guy, you idiot?

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.380
-Maybe I'll try catching this guy.
-That's nice.

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:42.150
-I'll send the reward back to my mom.
-What now?

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:45.590
Besides, now I kind of want to meet this rag demon.

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:48.590
I'll be off then.

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:51.160
-Hold on!
-Let her go, Hamsa.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:55.060
See you.

00:12:57.430 --> 00:13:02.540
Honestly, since when do gods
have to put up with this kind of treatment?

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:04.140
Idiots.

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:50.520
Come out, rag demon!

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:19.550
Surrender yourself, rag demon.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.550
I see that you are still obnoxious.

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:43.340
Now, where am I gonna find this demon?

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:49.480
Was that...?

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.130
Wait!

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:16.570
Stop!

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:21.170
What is this?

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:22.840
I'll tell you what this is.

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:24.850
You're my trophy.

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:47.730
This way! After him!

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:53.440
Are you okay?

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:59.650
I can't seem to get this free.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:08.360
-What is it?
-It's nothing!

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.230
I'm sorry.

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:15.760
Captain!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.370
Bye.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:27.570
Are you hurt, sir?

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:29.340
I'm fine.

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:30.580
Curses.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:33.250
Was that girl with the rag demon?

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:36.250
-After her! After the girl!
-Yes, my Lord.

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:56.640
Where did he run off to?

00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:00.510
Hey, you.

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:04.210
Do you see a demon in rags from up there?

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:08.480
Then would you let me switch places with you?

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:24.600
Found him.

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:31.240
-What?
-The girl on the tower is with him!

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:32.440
Don't let her get away!

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:34.270
Fire!

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:48.820
Damn it. Why is she getting attacked?

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:10.280
Those wings....

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:13.880
Mugaro, are you okay?

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.390
Who the hell are you?

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:32.790
What is it?

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:35.500
Do you think the rag demon summoned it?

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:47.010
Hold your positions!

00:19:47.140 --> 00:19:48.810
-Fire!
-Fire!

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:52.710
Retreat! Fall back! Fall back!

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:36.750
Where am I?

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:45.190
Good morning.

00:23:53.920 --> 00:23:57.690
-It is I, Kaisar Lidfard!
-And Charioce XVII too.

00:23:57.820 --> 00:23:59.330
-That was crude.
-What did you say?

00:23:59.660 --> 00:24:01.630
Shall we say it together?

00:24:01.760 --> 00:24:06.070
Next time on Rage of Bahamut: Virgin Soul,
"The Miserables."

00:24:06.200 --> 00:24:08.030
I can't believe I pronounced it right.

00:24:08.170 --> 00:24:10.770
Baha Soul!!

00:24:10.900 --> 00:24:13.040
Baha Baha Baha Soul!

00:24:13.170 --> 00:24:17.110
Tune in next time!
